{# Plate figure: 1-6 photographs in a grid, gaps transparent so the section
   ground shows through. The gap is the design, not padding.

   Images are {src, alt} only. `src` is the slug path with no width and no
   extension — the macro appends both, because the source set is a property of
   the pipeline (scripts/make-plates.js), not of the page.

   AVIF carries the srcset; the <img> is the WebP fallback and exists at 600
   only. See the note in make-plates.js: a 1200px WebP of a dense aerial cannot
   meet the 200KB cap at a quality worth shipping, and every browser that would
   choose the 1200px file supports AVIF.

   The fourth argument overrides `sizes`. The default assumes the plate spans
   the full 74rem wrap with nothing beside it — which, since the rail landed, is
   true of no current call site: the homepage plates sit in a half-width
   .figure-pair column, the inner-page plates share the row with a 20rem rail,
   and a rail plate is the rail's own width. A
   `sizes` that is too wide is not cosmetic: a 183px cell declared as 422px
   fetches the 1200px file at DPR 2, which is the waste this srcset exists to
   remove. Call sites in a narrower container must pass their own.

   Usage:
     {% from "components/image-grid.njk" import grid %}
     {{ grid([{src:"/img/plates/tea-canopy-plucking-table", alt:"..."}],
             "Caption text", "I") }}
#}
{% macro grid(images, caption, plate, sizes) %}
{%- set n = images | length -%}
{#- Column count at >=52rem. Below that the CSS is 1 or 2 columns. -#}
{%- set cols = 1 if n == 1 else (2 if n in [2, 4] else 3) -%}
{#- 1184px is --wrap (74rem) at its cap, less the page padding. -#}
{%- set sizes = sizes or ("(min-width: 52rem) " + (1184 // cols) + "px, " + ("100vw" if cols == 1 else "50vw")) -%}
<figure class="plate plate--{{ n }}">
  <div class="plate__grid">
    {% for im in images %}
    <picture class="plate__cell">
      <source type="image/avif" sizes="{{ sizes }}"
              srcset="{{ im.src }}-600.avif 600w, {{ im.src }}-1200.avif 1200w">
      <img src="{{ im.src }}-600.webp" alt="{{ im.alt }}"
           width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    </picture>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% if caption %}
  <figcaption class="plate__caption">
    {% if plate %}<span class="plate__no">Plate {{ plate }}</span>{% endif %}{{ caption }}
  </figcaption>
  {% endif %}
</figure>
{% endmacro %}
